{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>Then you shall investigate and search out.</b> In cases involving capital punishment they examine the witnesses through seven interrogations (חקירות): in which sabbatical cycle, in which year, in which month, on what day of the month, on which day of the week, at which hour of the day, in which place. And further they examine them through seven inquiries (בדיקות), and the inquiries are matters that are not essential to the testimony and the testimony does not depend on them — that is, they ask them: what was the garment worn by the slain or the slayer, white or black; the soil of the ground on which he was slain — was it white or red. An incident occurred where witnesses said: in such-and-such a place, under the fig tree, so-and-so killed the person; and the Sages examined the witnesses and said to them: were its figs black or white, were their stems long or short. And the secret of the seven interrogations corresponds to the seven extremities, and the seventh is the Hall of Holiness aligned in the center, and it is the truth that decides — thus the truth is known through the seven interrogations."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:48:10.329552146Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}